{"nodes": [{"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "label": "PyChrono technology reference", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_swig", "label": "SWIG wrapping layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PyChrono is a set of Python modules mirroring Chrono units, generated through SWIG; SWIG's limitations (no nested classes, no templates) directly shape the Python API surface."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_templated_class_aliases", "label": "Templated classes wrapped as named specializations", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Python has no template support, so each relevant C++ specialization is wrapped under its C++ alias name (ChVector3d, ChQuaterniond, ChMatrixDynamicd, ChFramed...). std::vector containers get a vector_ prefix, e.g. chrono.vector_ChVector3d for std::vector<ChVector<double>>."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_object_lifetime", "label": "Python object creation and assignment semantics", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is only one creation form in Python and lifetime is managed automatically, removing the C++ stack-vs-heap choice and the matching delete. The = operator assigns another handle rather than copying, so two names can refer to one ChSystem."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_shared_pointers", "label": "Shared pointers handled automatically", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chrono's C++ shared pointers are template-based and templates are unsupported in Python, but this is not an issue because PyChrono handles shared-pointer objects automatically: constructing the Python object also creates the referenced object, and further handles are made by plain assignment."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_vector_member_access", "label": "ChVector x/y/z as members instead of accessor calls", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The C++ x()/y()/z() reference-returning accessors are mapped to direct member access in Python to avoid issues with returning references; the same applies to quaternion components e0..e3."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_downcasting", "label": "Upcasting vs manual downcasting (CastToXXX)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Upcasting of derived to base works automatically, including for shared pointers. Downcasting is the hard direction: it is automatic only for classes derived from ChFunction and ChAsset, otherwise the user calls a CastToXXX() helper, the Python analogue of dynamic_cast<derived>(base)."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_nested_class_flattening", "label": "Nested class flattening", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SWIG does not support nested classes in Python, so instead of ignoring them PyChrono flattens every nested Chrono class into the upper namespace level; nested enum classes become underscore-joined names such as VisualizationType_MESH."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_unmapped_classes", "label": "Detecting unmapped C++ classes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A correctly wrapped return value echoes as a pychrono type proxying a Swig Object; an unmapped one echoes only as a bare Swig Object pointer and is unusable from Python. This gives users a concrete test for coverage gaps to report."}], "edges": [{"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_introduction_pychrono", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_swig", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_object_lifetime", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_templated_class_aliases", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_shared_pointers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_vector_member_access", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_downcasting", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_nested_class_flattening", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_pychrono_reference", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_unmapped_classes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_swig", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_nested_class_flattening", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_swig", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_templated_class_aliases", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_templated_class_aliases", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_shared_pointers", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pychrono/pychrono_reference.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_object_lifetime", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_pychrono_pychrono_reference_shared_pointers", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/pych